%%text South Wind- words by Donal O?Sullivan
%%text South wind of the gentle rain, you banish winter weather
%%text Bring salmon to the pool again, the bees among the heather
%%text If northward now you mean to blow as you rustle soft above me
%%text Godspeed be with you as you go with a kiss for those that love me
%%text 
%%text From south I come with velvet breeze, my word all nature blesses
%%text I melt the snow and strew the leas with flowers and soft caresses
%%text I?ll help you to dispel your woes, with joy I?ll take your greeting
%%text And bear to it to your loved Mayo upon my wings so fleeting
%%text 
%%text My Connacht famed for wine and play, so gay, so loyal, so loving
%%text Here?s my fond kiss I?ll send today borne on the wind in its roving
%%text These Munster folks are good and kind, right royally they treat me
%%text But this land I?ll gladly leave behind with your Connacht pipes to greet me


